CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[main\.loop_invariant_step\.\d+\] line \d+ Check invariant after step for loop main\.\d+: FAILURE$
--
--
Checks that a variable that a loop invariant reads is not a loop local: the
invariant is evaluated at the loop head, where the variable holds the value of
the previous iteration.
